## Correctness — 60 % · 1 error(s)

- **Error** — operationId “getPet” is used by more than one operation.
  \`GET /pet/{petId}\` · \`/paths/~1pet~1{petId}/get\`
  *Why it matters*: An operationId must be unique in the document, and this documentation turns it into the operation's deep link: one of the two links lands on the other operation. Rename one of them.

## Docs readiness — 74 % · 1 warning(s) · 1 note(s)

- **Warning** — Security scheme “apiKey” has no description.
  \`components.securitySchemes.apiKey\` · \`/components/securitySchemes/apiKey\`
  *Why it matters*: The credentials block shows that description to explain what to paste and where to get it. Without one, the reader faces a bare field labelled with the scheme's key.
- **Note** — This operation carries no tag.
  \`DELETE /admin/reset\` · (Hidden operation) · \`/paths/~1admin~1reset/delete\`
  *Why it matters*: It lands in the navigation's catch-all group along with every other untagged operation, and the reader cannot tell which family it belongs to. Give it at least one tag.
"
